        <num>25-242-F</num>
        <codify:insert history="false" doc="Code of Maryland Regulations" path="01|02|04" before="annos" codified:doc="Code of Maryland Regulations" codified:path="01|02|04|.22">
          <section cache:ref-path="01|02|04|.22">
            <prefix>Regulation</prefix>
            <num>.22</num>
            <heading>Late Fee Waiver or Suspension.</heading>
            <para>
              <num>A.</num>
              <text>A charitable organization may request the Secretary of State to waive or suspend a late fee.</text>
            </para>
            <para>
              <num>B.</num>
              <text>A request to waive or suspend a late fee must:</text>
              <para>
                <num>(1)</num>
                <text>Be in writing;</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(2)</num>
                <text>Explain the cause or causes of the charitable organization’s late filing; and</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(3)</num>
                <text>To the extent such late filing was reasonably preventable, explain what has been or will be done to prevent future late filings.</text>
              </para>
            </para>
            <para>
              <num>C.</num>
              <text>In addition to the written request submitted in accordance with <cite path="01|02|04|.22|B." doc="Code of Maryland Regulations">§B of this regulation</cite>, the Secretary of State may consider, among other factors and without limitation, the following when determining whether to grant a request to waive or suspend some or all of a late fee:</text>
              <para>
                <num>(1)</num>
                <text>Whether the charitable organization has submitted all required outstanding annual reports to the Secretary of State;</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(2)</num>
                <text>Whether the charitable organization’s registration history includes previous late filings;</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(3)</num>
                <text>Whether the charitable organization already paid some of the late fee;</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(4)</num>
                <text>Whether the charitable organization previously asked for and was granted a late fee waiver or suspension; and</text>
              </para>
              <para>
                <num>(5)</num>
                <text>Whether the charitable organization has the ability to pay the late fee.</text>
              </para>
            </para>
            <para>
              <num>D.</num>
              <text>If the Secretary of State makes a determination to waive or suspend some of the late fee, the charitable organization must pay any remaining late fee within 30 days of notification of the Secretary’s decision.</text>
            </para>
            <para>
              <num>E.</num>
              <text>Failure of a charitable organization to fully comply after being granted partial waiver or suspension of a late fee will result in revocation of the late fee waiver or suspension.</text>
            </para>
            <para>
              <num>F.</num>
              <text>A partial or complete denial of a late fee waiver or suspension request is not an adverse action under <cite path="01.02.03.05" doc="Code of Maryland Regulations">COMAR 01.02.03.05</cite>.</text>
            </para>
          </section>
        </codify:insert>
